<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penobscot</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Penobscot are an Algonquian-speaking Indigenous people of the Penobscot river valley in Maine, members of the Wabanaki Confederacy. Under leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madockawando">Madockawando</a> they traded with and fought both the French and the English in the colonial wars. Their reservation is centred on Indian Island near Old Town, and with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passamaquoddy">Passamaquoddy</a> they secured the Maine Indian Claims Settlement Act of 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penobscot.jpg" alt="Penobscot" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Penobscotlogo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
